// Stats-based win probability formula -- league-wide ranking.
// Paste into Kibana Dev Tools Console (or the ES|QL tab) to run.
//
// This is a transparent, documented heuristic -- see docs/model.md for the
// reasoning behind the weights. It is NOT a trained ML model.
//
//   raw_score = (net_rating * 0.5)
//             + (last_10_win_pct * 30)
//             + (home_court_bonus)   // +5 if this is the home team, else 0
//
// This query deliberately omits the home-court bonus: it ranks teams in the
// abstract, with no game attached, so there is no home team to give it to.
// The bonus is applied in esql/matchup_comparison.esql and
// esql/value_mismatches.esql, both of which join against a specific game.
// Expect the numbers here to sit ~5 points below the ones the agent quotes
// for a home team -- that gap is the bonus, not a bug.
//
// raw_score is not a probability and is not on a 0-100 scale. Converting a
// PAIR of raw_scores into a probability happens in the agent's reasoning
// step (agent_builder/setup.md), because ES|QL has no exp(). Run
// scripts/reference_model.py to see the expected conversion for the sample
// docs.

FROM nba_team_stats
// Guard the division: a team with no last-10 record (preseason, or a
// backfill gap in ingest) would otherwise divide by zero and land at null,
// silently dropping out of the ranking. 0.5 means "no information, treat as
// average" -- 0.0 would punish the team for a data problem.
| EVAL last_10_games = last_10_wins + last_10_losses
| EVAL last_10_win_pct = CASE(
    last_10_games == 0,
    0.5,
    TO_DOUBLE(last_10_wins) / TO_DOUBLE(last_10_games)
  )
| EVAL raw_score = (net_rating * 0.5) + (last_10_win_pct * 30)
| EVAL raw_score = ROUND(raw_score, 2)
| KEEP team, team_abbreviation, season, net_rating, last_10_wins, last_10_losses, last_10_win_pct, raw_score
| SORT raw_score DESC
